> This isn't just windows, it's like that on macos also. Using ghostty takes almost 10 seconds to load. Wezterm is much faster but still noticeably slower since their last big update.

@hijoe @MFattakhov @scratchmex   Are you using the opencode system theme? I switched away from the system theme and the sluggishness went away immediately. The mismatch is likely in functions like `getTerminalBackgroundColor:app.tsx:44-102`

It can't all be here, as the timeout here is only 1 second, but I think there is a mismatch between the escape sequences that ghostty sends and what we are expecting. Let me know if switching themes resolves your issues as well.

